export const JOHN_OVERRIDES: Readonly<Record<string, string>> = {
  "1:2": "He was in the beginning with God.",
  "1:7": "This man came as a witness, to give testimony of the light, so that all men might believe through him.",
  "1:9": "That was the true light, which enlightens every man who comes into this world.",
  "1:12": "But as many as received him, he gave them power to be made the sons of God, to those who believe in his name.",
  "1:15": "John bears witness of him and cries out, saying: This was he of whom I spoke: He who shall come after me is preferred before me: because he was before me.",
  "1:16": "And of his fullness we have all received: and grace for grace.",
  "1:18": "No one has seen God at any time: the only begotten Son, who is in the bosom of the Father, he has made him known.",
  "1:22": "They said therefore to him: Who are you, so that we may give an answer to those who sent us? What do you say of yourself?",
  "1:24": "And those who had been sent were of the Pharisees.",
  "1:25": "And they asked him and said to him: Why then do you baptize, if you are not the Christ, nor Elias, nor the prophet?",
  "1:26": "John answered them, saying: I baptize with water: but there has stood one in your midst whom you do not know.",
  "1:27": "He is the one who shall come after me, who is preferred before me: the strap of whose sandal I am not worthy to untie.",
  "1:29": "The next day, John saw Jesus coming to him; and he said: Behold the Lamb of God. Behold him who takes away the sin of the world.",
  "1:31": "And I did not know him: but so that he may be made known to Israel, that is why I have come baptizing with water.",
  "1:32": "And John gave testimony, saying: I saw the Spirit coming down like a dove from heaven; and he remained upon him.",
  "1:33": "And I did not know him: but he who sent me to baptize with water said to me: He upon whom you shall see the Spirit descending and remaining, he is the one who baptizes with the Holy Spirit.",
  "1:35": "The next day again John was standing there with two of his disciples.",
  "1:36": "And looking at Jesus as he walked, he said: Behold the Lamb of God.",
  "1:38": "And Jesus, turning and seeing them following him, said to them: What are you looking for? They said to him: Rabbi (which means, translated, Master), where do you live?",
  "1:39": "He said to them: Come and see. They came and saw where he lived: and they stayed with him that day. Now it was about the tenth hour.",
  "1:40": "And Andrew, the brother of Simon Peter, was one of the two who had heard John and followed him.",
  "1:41": "He first found his brother Simon and said to him: We have found the Messias, which is, translated, the Christ.",
  "1:42": "And he brought him to Jesus. And Jesus, looking at him, said: You are Simon the son of Jona. You shall be called Cephas, which is translated Peter.",
  "1:43": "On the following day, he wanted to go into Galilee: and he found Philip. And Jesus said to him: Follow me.",
  "1:45": "Philip found Nathanael and said to him: We have found him of whom Moses in the law and the prophets wrote, Jesus the son of Joseph of Nazareth.",
  "1:46": "And Nathanael said to him: Can anything good come from Nazareth? Philip said to him: Come and see.",
  "1:47": "Jesus saw Nathanael coming to him, and he said of him: Behold an Israelite indeed, in whom there is no guile.",
  "1:48": "Nathanael said to him: How do you know me? Jesus answered and said to him: Before Philip called you, when you were under the fig tree, I saw you.",
  "1:49": "Nathanael answered him and said: Rabbi, you are the Son of God. You are the King of Israel.",
  "1:50": "Jesus answered and said to him: Because I said to you, I saw you under the fig tree, you believe: you shall see greater things than these.",
  "1:51": "And he said to him: Amen, amen, I say to you, you shall see heaven opened and the angels of God ascending and descending upon the Son of man.",
  "2:1": "And on the third day, there was a wedding in Cana of Galilee: and the mother of Jesus was there.",
  "2:2": "And Jesus also was invited, and his disciples, to the wedding.",
  "2:3": "And when the wine ran short, the mother of Jesus said to him: They have no wine.",
  "2:4": "And Jesus said to her: Woman, what is that to me and to you? My hour is not yet come.",
  "2:5": "His mother said to the servants: Whatever he shall say to you, do it.",
  "2:6": "Now there were set there six stone water jars, according to the Jewish custom of purifying, each holding two or three measures.",
  "2:7": "Jesus said to them: Fill the water jars with water. And they filled them up to the brim.",
  "2:8": "And Jesus said to them: Draw some out now and take it to the chief steward of the feast. And they took it.",
  "2:9": "And when the chief steward had tasted the water made wine and did not know where it came from, but the servants who had drawn the water knew, the chief steward called the bridegroom,",
  "2:10": "And said to him: Every man at first sets out the good wine, and when men have drunk freely, then what is worse. But you have kept the good wine until now.",
  "2:11": "This beginning of miracles Jesus did in Cana of Galilee and showed his glory. And his disciples believed in him.",
  "2:14": "And he found in the temple those who sold oxen and sheep and doves, and the money changers sitting there.",
  "2:15": "And when he had made a kind of whip of little cords, he drove them all out of the temple, the sheep also and the oxen: and he poured out the money of the changers and overturned their tables.",
  "2:16": "And to those who sold doves he said: Take these things away from here, and do not make the house of my Father a house of trade.",
  "2:17": "And his disciples remembered that it was written: The zeal of your house has eaten me up.",
  "2:18": "The Jews, therefore, answered and said to him: What sign do you show us, seeing that you do these things?",
  "2:20": "The Jews then said: This temple was forty-six years in building; and will you raise it up in three days?",
  "2:22": "When therefore he had risen again from the dead, his disciples remembered that he had said this: and they believed the scripture and the word that Jesus had said.",
  "2:23": "Now when he was in Jerusalem at the pasch, on the festival day, many believed in his name, seeing his signs which he did.",
  "2:24": "But Jesus did not trust himself to them, because he knew all men,",
  "2:25": "And because he did not need anyone to give testimony about man: for he knew what was in man.",
  "3:2": "This man came to Jesus by night and said to him: Rabbi, we know that you have come from God as a teacher; for no one can do these signs which you do, unless God is with him.",
  "3:4": "Nicodemus said to him: How can a man be born when he is old? Can he enter a second time into his mother's womb and be born again?",
  "3:6": "What is born of the flesh is flesh: and what is born of the Spirit is spirit.",
  "3:7": "Do not wonder that I said to you: You must be born again.",
  "3:8": "The Spirit breathes where he will, and you hear his voice: but you do not know where he comes from or where he goes. So is everyone who is born of the Spirit.",
  "3:10": "Jesus answered and said to him: Are you a master in Israel, and do you not know these things?",
  "3:11": "Amen, amen, I say to you that we speak what we know and we testify to what we have seen: and you do not receive our testimony.",
  "3:12": "If I have spoken to you of earthly things, and you do not believe, how will you believe if I speak to you of heavenly things?",
  "3:13": "And no one has ascended into heaven, except he who descended from heaven, the Son of man who is in heaven.",
  "3:17": "For God did not send his Son into the world to judge the world: but so that the world may be saved by him.",
  "3:18": "Whoever believes in him is not judged. But whoever does not believe is already judged: because he does not believe in the name of the only begotten Son of God.",
  "3:19": "And this is the judgment: that the light has come into the world, and men loved darkness rather than the light: for their works were evil.",
  "3:20": "For everyone who does evil hates the light and does not come to the light, so that his works may not be exposed.",
  "3:21": "But whoever does the truth comes to the light, so that his works may be made known: because they are done in God.",
  "3:22": "After these things, Jesus and his disciples came into the land of Judea: and there he stayed with them and baptized.",
  "3:24": "For John had not yet been thrown into prison.",
  "3:25": "And a dispute arose between some of John's disciples and the Jews about purification.",
  "3:26": "And they came to John and said to him: Rabbi, he who was with you beyond the Jordan, to whom you gave testimony: behold, he is baptizing and all men are coming to him.",
  "3:27": "John answered and said: A man cannot receive anything unless it is given him from heaven.",
  "3:28": "You yourselves bear me witness that I said that I am not the Christ, but that I am sent before him.",
  "3:29": "He who has the bride is the bridegroom: but the friend of the bridegroom, who stands and hears him, rejoices greatly because of the bridegroom's voice. This my joy therefore is fulfilled.",
  "3:31": "He who comes from above is above all. He who is of the earth, of the earth he is, and of the earth he speaks. He who comes from heaven is above all.",
  "3:32": "And what he has seen and heard, to that he testifies: and no one receives his testimony.",
  "3:33": "Whoever has received his testimony has set his seal to this, that God is true.",
  "3:36": "Whoever believes in the Son has life everlasting: but whoever does not believe the Son shall not see life: but the wrath of God remains on him.",
  "4:1": "When Jesus therefore learned that the Pharisees had heard that Jesus was making and baptizing more disciples than John",
  "4:4": "And he had to pass through Samaria.",
  "4:5": "He came therefore to a city of Samaria which is called Sichar, near the land which Jacob gave to his son Joseph.",
  "4:6": "Now Jacob's well was there. Jesus therefore, being tired from his journey, sat down by the well. It was about the sixth hour.",
  "4:7": "A woman of Samaria came to draw water. Jesus said to her: Give me a drink.",
  "4:8": "For his disciples had gone into the city to buy food.",
  "4:9": "Then that Samaritan woman said to him: How is it that you, being a Jew, ask a drink of me, who am a Samaritan woman? For the Jews have no dealings with the Samaritans.",
  "4:10": "Jesus answered and said to her: If you knew the gift of God, and who it is that says to you: Give me a drink; you perhaps would have asked of him, and he would have given you living water.",
  "4:11": "The woman said to him: Sir, you have nothing with which to draw, and the well is deep. Where then do you get living water?",
  "4:12": "Are you greater than our father Jacob, who gave us the well and drank from it, himself and his children and his cattle?",
  "4:13": "Jesus answered and said to her: Whoever drinks of this water shall thirst again: but whoever drinks of the water that I will give him shall not thirst for ever.",
  "4:15": "The woman said to him: Sir, give me this water, so that I may not thirst, nor come here to draw.",
  "4:16": "Jesus said to her: Go, call your husband, and come here.",
  "4:17": "The woman answered and said: I have no husband. Jesus said to her: You have said well: I have no husband.",
  "4:18": "For you have had five husbands: and he whom you now have is not your husband. This you have said truly.",
  "4:19": "The woman said to him: Sir, I see that you are a prophet.",
  "4:21": "Jesus said to her: Woman, believe me, the hour is coming when you shall adore the Father neither on this mountain nor in Jerusalem.",
  "4:22": "You adore what you do not know: we adore what we know. For salvation is from the Jews.",
  "4:23": "But the hour is coming, and now is, when the true adorers shall adore the Father in spirit and in truth. For the Father also seeks such to adore him.",
  "4:24": "God is a spirit: and those who adore him must adore him in spirit and in truth.",
  "4:25": "The woman said to him: I know that the Messias is coming (who is called Christ): therefore, when he comes, he will tell us all things.",
  "4:26": "Jesus said to her: I am he, who am speaking with you.",
  "4:27": "And at that moment his disciples came. And they wondered that he was talking with the woman. Yet no one said: What do you seek? Or: Why do you talk with her?",
  "4:28": "The woman therefore left her water jar and went her way into the city and said to the men there:",
  "4:29": "Come and see a man who has told me all the things I have done. Is not he the Christ?",
  "4:30": "They went out of the city therefore and came to him.",
  "4:31": "In the meantime, the disciples urged him, saying: Rabbi, eat.",
  "4:32": "But he said to them: I have food to eat which you do not know.",
  "4:33": "The disciples therefore said to one another: Has anyone brought him something to eat?",
  "4:34": "Jesus said to them: My food is to do the will of him who sent me, so that I may finish his work.",
  "4:35": "Do you not say: There are still four months, and then the harvest comes? Behold, I say to you, lift up your eyes and look at the fields. For they are already white for harvest.",
  "4:36": "And he who reaps receives wages and gathers fruit for life everlasting: so that both he who sows and he who reaps may rejoice together.",
  "4:37": "For in this the saying is true: One man sows, and another reaps.",
  "4:38": "I have sent you to reap what you did not labor for. Others have labored: and you have entered into their labors.",
  "4:39": "Now many of the Samaritans of that city believed in him because of the word of the woman giving testimony: He told me all the things I have done.",
  "4:40": "So when the Samaritans had come to him, they asked him to stay there. And he stayed there two days.",
  "4:41": "And many more believed in him because of his own word.",
  "4:42": "And they said to the woman: We now believe, not because of what you said: for we ourselves have heard him and know that this is indeed the Savior of the world.",
  "4:45": "And when he had come into Galilee, the Galileans welcomed him, having seen all the things he had done in Jerusalem on the festival day: for they also had gone to the festival day.",
  "4:46": "He came again therefore into Cana of Galilee, where he made the water wine. And there was a certain official whose son was sick at Capernaum.",
  "4:47": "When he heard that Jesus had come from Judea into Galilee, he went to him and begged him to come down and heal his son: for he was at the point of death.",
  "4:48": "Jesus therefore said to him: Unless you see signs and wonders, you do not believe.",
  "4:49": "The official said to him: Lord, come down before my son dies.",
  "4:50": "Jesus said to him: Go your way. Your son lives. The man believed the word which Jesus said to him and went his way.",
  "4:51": "And as he was going down, his servants met him: and they brought word, saying that his son was alive.",
  "4:52": "He asked them therefore the hour at which he grew better. And they said to him: Yesterday at the seventh hour the fever left him.",
  "4:53": "The father therefore knew that it was at the same hour that Jesus said to him: Your son lives. And he himself believed, and his whole household.",
  "4:54": "This again was the second miracle that Jesus did, when he had come out of Judea into Galilee.",
  "5:1": "After these things there was a festival day of the Jews: and Jesus went up to Jerusalem.",
  "5:3": "In these lay a great crowd of sick people, of blind, of lame, of withered, waiting for the moving of the water.",
  "5:4": "And an angel of the Lord came down at certain times into the pond, and the water was stirred. And whoever went down first into the pond after the stirring of the water was made whole of whatever sickness he had.",
  "5:5": "And there was a certain man there who had been sick for thirty-eight years.",
  "5:6": "When Jesus saw him lying there and knew that he had been sick a long time, he said to him: Do you want to be made whole?",
  "5:7": "The sick man answered him: Sir, I have no one to put me into the pond when the water is stirred. For while I am coming, another goes down before me.",
  "5:8": "Jesus said to him: Arise, take up your bed and walk.",
  "5:10": "The Jews therefore said to the man who was healed: It is the sabbath. It is not lawful for you to take up your bed.",
  "5:11": "He answered them: He who made me whole said to me: Take up your bed and walk.",
  "5:13": "But the man who was healed did not know who it was: for Jesus had slipped away from the crowd that was in the place.",
  "5:14": "Afterwards, Jesus found him in the temple and said to him: Behold, you are made whole: sin no more, so that nothing worse happens to you.",
  "5:16": "That is why the Jews persecuted Jesus, because he did these things on the sabbath.",
  "5:17": "But Jesus answered them: My Father works until now; and I work.",
  "5:18": "For this reason therefore the Jews tried all the more to kill him, because he not only broke the sabbath but also said God was his Father, making himself equal to God. Then Jesus answered and said to them:",
  "5:19": "Amen, amen, I say to you, the Son cannot do anything of himself, but only what he sees the Father doing: for whatever he does, the Son also does in the same way.",
  "5:20": "For the Father loves the Son and shows him all things which he himself does: and he will show him greater works than these, so that you may wonder.",
  "5:22": "For the Father does not judge anyone: but has given all judgment to the Son,",
  "5:23": "So that all men may honor the Son, as they honor the Father. He who does not honor the Son does not honor the Father who has sent him.",
  "5:24": "Amen, amen, I say to you that he who hears my word and believes him who sent me has life everlasting: and does not come into judgment, but has passed from death to life.",
  "5:25": "Amen, amen, I say to you that the hour is coming, and now is, when the dead shall hear the voice of the Son of God: and those who hear shall live.",
  "5:27": "And he has given him power to carry out judgment, because he is the Son of man.",
  "5:28": "Do not wonder at this: for the hour is coming in which all who are in the graves shall hear the voice of the Son of God.",
  "5:29": "And those who have done good things shall come forth to the resurrection of life: but those who have done evil, to the resurrection of judgment.",
  "5:30": "I cannot do anything of myself. As I hear, so I judge. And my judgment is just: because I do not seek my own will, but the will of him who sent me.",
  "5:32": "There is another who bears witness of me: and I know that the witness which he gives of me is true.",
  "5:34": "But I do not receive testimony from man: but I say these things so that you may be saved.",
  "5:36": "But I have a greater testimony than that of John: for the works which the Father has given me to complete, the very works which I do, give testimony of me, that the Father has sent me.",
  "5:37": "And the Father himself who has sent me has given testimony of me: you have never heard his voice, nor seen his form.",
  "5:38": "And you do not have his word abiding in you: for you do not believe him whom he has sent.",
  "5:39": "Search the scriptures: for you think that in them you have life everlasting. And they are the ones that give testimony of me.",
  "5:40": "And you will not come to me so that you may have life.",
  "5:41": "I do not receive glory from men.",
  "5:42": "But I know you, that you do not have the love of God in you.",
  "5:43": "I have come in the name of my Father, and you do not receive me: if another comes in his own name, him you will receive.",
  "5:44": "How can you believe, who receive glory from one another, and do not seek the glory which is from God alone?",
  "5:45": "Do not think that I will accuse you to the Father. There is one who accuses you, Moses, in whom you trust.",
  "5:46": "For if you believed Moses, you would perhaps believe me also: for he wrote of me.",
  "6:1": "After these things Jesus went across the sea of Galilee, which is the sea of Tiberias.",
  "6:2": "And a great crowd followed him, because they saw the miracles which he did on those who were sick.",
  "6:3": "Jesus therefore went up a mountain: and there he sat with his disciples.",
  "6:5": "When Jesus therefore had lifted up his eyes and seen that a very great crowd was coming to him, he said to Philip: Where shall we buy bread, so that these may eat?",
  "6:6": "And this he said to test him: for he himself knew what he would do.",
  "6:7": "Philip answered him: Two hundred pennies' worth of bread is not enough for them, for each one to take a little.",
  "6:8": "One of his disciples, Andrew, the brother of Simon Peter, said to him:",
  "6:9": "There is a boy here who has five barley loaves and two fish. But what are these among so many?",
  "6:10": "Then Jesus said: Make the men sit down. Now there was much grass in the place. The men therefore sat down, about five thousand in number.",
  "6:11": "And Jesus took the loaves: and when he had given thanks, he distributed them to those who were seated. In the same way also of the fish, as much as they wanted.",
  "6:12": "And when they were filled, he said to his disciples: Gather up the fragments that remain, so that nothing is lost.",
  "6:13": "They gathered them up therefore and filled twelve baskets with the fragments of the five barley loaves which were left over by those who had eaten.",
  "6:14": "Now those men, when they had seen what a miracle Jesus had done, said: This is truly the prophet who is to come into the world.",
  "6:15": "Jesus therefore, when he knew that they would come to take him by force and make him king, withdrew again into the mountain, himself alone.",
  "6:16": "And when evening had come, his disciples went down to the sea.",
  "6:17": "And when they had gotten into a boat, they went across the sea to Capernaum. And it was now dark: and Jesus had not come to them.",
  "6:18": "And the sea grew rough, because a strong wind was blowing.",
  "6:19": "When they had rowed therefore about twenty-five or thirty furlongs, they saw Jesus walking upon the sea and drawing near to the boat. And they were afraid.",
  "6:20": "But he said to them: It is I. Do not be afraid.",
  "6:21": "They were willing therefore to take him into the boat. And at once the boat was at the land to which they were going.",
  "6:22": "The next day, the crowd that stood on the other side of the sea saw that there was no other boat there but one: and that Jesus had not entered the boat with his disciples, but that his disciples had gone away alone.",
  "6:23": "But other boats came from Tiberias, near the place where they had eaten the bread after the Lord had given thanks.",
  "6:24": "When therefore the crowd saw that Jesus was not there, nor his disciples, they got into the boats and came to Capernaum, looking for Jesus.",
  "6:26": "Jesus answered them and said: Amen, amen, I say to you, you seek me, not because you have seen miracles, but because you ate of the loaves and were filled.",
  "6:27": "Do not labor for the food which perishes, but for that which endures to life everlasting, which the Son of man will give you. For on him God the Father has set his seal.",
  "6:28": "They said therefore to him: What shall we do, so that we may work the works of God?",
  "6:30": "They said therefore to him: What sign then do you show, so that we may see and may believe you? What work do you do?",
  "6:31": "Our fathers ate manna in the desert, as it is written: He gave them bread from heaven to eat.",
  "6:32": "Then Jesus said to them: Amen, amen, I say to you, Moses did not give you bread from heaven, but my Father gives you the true bread from heaven.",
  "6:35": "And Jesus said to them: I am the bread of life. Whoever comes to me shall not hunger: and whoever believes in me shall never thirst.",
  "6:36": "But I said to you that you also have seen me, and you do not believe.",
  "6:37": "All that the Father gives to me shall come to me: and whoever comes to me, I will not cast out.",
  "6:38": "Because I came down from heaven, not to do my own will but the will of him who sent me.",
  "6:39": "Now this is the will of the Father who sent me: that of all that he has given me, I should lose nothing, but should raise it up again on the last day.",
  "6:40": "And this is the will of my Father who sent me: that everyone who sees the Son and believes in him may have life everlasting. And I will raise him up on the last day.",
  "6:41": "The Jews therefore murmured about him, because he had said: I am the living bread which came down from heaven.",
  "6:42": "And they said: Is not this Jesus, the son of Joseph, whose father and mother we know? How then does he say: I came down from heaven?",
  "6:43": "Jesus therefore answered and said to them: Do not murmur among yourselves.",
  "6:44": "No one can come to me unless the Father, who has sent me, draws him. And I will raise him up on the last day.",
  "6:45": "It is written in the prophets: And they shall all be taught by God. Everyone who has heard of the Father and has learned comes to me.",
  "6:46": "Not that anyone has seen the Father: but he who is from God, he has seen the Father.",
  "6:47": "Amen, amen, I say to you: Whoever believes in me has everlasting life.",
  "6:49": "Your fathers ate manna in the desert: and they died.",
  "6:50": "This is the bread which comes down from heaven, so that if anyone eats of it, he may not die.",
  "6:52": "If anyone eats of this bread, he shall live for ever: and the bread that I will give is my flesh, for the life of the world.",
  "6:53": "The Jews therefore argued among themselves, saying: How can this man give us his flesh to eat?",
  "6:54": "Then Jesus said to them: Amen, amen, I say to you: unless you eat the flesh of the Son of man and drink his blood, you shall not have life in you.",
  "6:55": "Whoever eats my flesh and drinks my blood has everlasting life: and I will raise him up on the last day.",
  "6:56": "For my flesh is food indeed: and my blood is drink indeed.",
  "6:57": "Whoever eats my flesh and drinks my blood abides in me: and I in him.",
  "6:58": "As the living Father has sent me and I live by the Father: so whoever eats me, he also shall live by me.",
  "6:59": "This is the bread that came down from heaven. Not as your fathers ate manna and died. Whoever eats this bread shall live for ever.",
  "6:61": "Many therefore of his disciples, hearing it, said: This saying is hard; and who can listen to it?",
  "6:62": "But Jesus, knowing in himself that his disciples were murmuring at this, said to them: Does this scandalize you?",
  "6:63": "What then if you should see the Son of man ascend up where he was before?",
  "6:64": "It is the spirit that gives life: the flesh profits nothing. The words that I have spoken to you are spirit and life.",
  "6:65": "But there are some of you who do not believe. For Jesus knew from the beginning who they were that did not believe and who it was that would betray him.",
  "6:66": "And he said: That is why I said to you that no one can come to me unless it is given him by my Father.",
  "6:67": "After this, many of his disciples went back and no longer walked with him.",
  "6:71": "Jesus answered them: Have I not chosen you twelve? And one of you is a devil.",
  "6:72": "Now he meant Judas Iscariot, the son of Simon: for this same man was about to betray him, though he was one of the twelve.",
  "7:1": "After these things, Jesus walked in Galilee: for he would not walk in Judea, because the Jews were seeking to kill him.",
  "7:2": "Now the Jewish feast of tabernacles was at hand.",
  "7:3": "And his brethren said to him: Leave here and go into Judea, so that your disciples also may see the works which you do.",
  "7:4": "For no one does anything in secret if he himself wants to be known openly. If you do these things, show yourself to the world.",
  "7:6": "Then Jesus said to them: My time has not yet come; but your time is always ready.",
  "7:7": "The world cannot hate you: but it hates me, because I give testimony of it, that its works are evil.",
  "7:8": "You go up to this festival day: but I am not going up to this festival day, because my time is not yet fulfilled.",
  "7:10": "But after his brethren had gone up, then he also went up to the feast, not openly, but as it were in secret.",
  "7:11": "The Jews therefore were looking for him on the festival day and said: Where is he?",
  "7:12": "And there was much murmuring among the crowd about him. For some said: He is a good man. And others said: No, but he leads the people astray.",
  "7:14": "Now about the middle of the feast, Jesus went up into the temple and taught.",
  "7:15": "And the Jews wondered, saying: How does this man know letters, having never studied?",
  "7:16": "Jesus answered them and said: My teaching is not mine, but his who sent me.",
  "7:17": "If anyone will do his will, he shall know of the teaching, whether it is from God, or whether I speak of myself.",
  "7:18": "He who speaks of himself seeks his own glory: but he who seeks the glory of him who sent him, he is true and there is no injustice in him.",
  "7:20": "Why do you seek to kill me? The crowd answered and said: You have a devil. Who is seeking to kill you?",
  "7:21": "Jesus answered and said to them: I have done one work: and you all wonder.",
  "7:22": "Moses gave you circumcision (not that it is from Moses, but from the fathers): and on the sabbath day you circumcise a man.",
  "7:23": "If a man receives circumcision on the sabbath day, so that the law of Moses may not be broken, are you angry with me because I have healed the whole man on the sabbath day?",
  "7:24": "Do not judge according to appearance: but judge with just judgment.",
  "7:25": "Some therefore of the people of Jerusalem said: Is not this he whom they seek to kill?",
  "7:26": "And behold, he speaks openly: and they say nothing to him. Have the rulers truly come to know that this is the Christ?",
  "7:27": "But we know where this man is from: but when the Christ comes, no one knows where he is from.",
  "7:28": "Jesus therefore cried out in the temple, teaching and saying: You both know me, and you know where I am from. And I have not come of myself: but he who sent me is true, whom you do not know.",
  "7:30": "They tried therefore to seize him: and no one laid hands on him, because his hour had not yet come.",
  "7:31": "But many of the people believed in him and said: When the Christ comes, will he do more miracles than this man does?",
  "7:32": "The Pharisees heard the people murmuring these things about him: and the rulers and Pharisees sent officers to seize him.",
  "7:33": "Jesus therefore said to them: Yet a little while I am with you: and then I go to him who sent me.",
  "7:35": "The Jews therefore said among themselves: Where will he go, that we shall not find him? Will he go to those scattered among the Gentiles and teach the Gentiles?",
  "7:37": "And on the last and great day of the feast, Jesus stood and cried out, saying: If anyone thirsts, let him come to me and drink.",
  "7:38": "Whoever believes in me, as the scripture says: Out of his belly shall flow rivers of living water.",
  "7:39": "Now this he said of the Spirit which those who believed in him were to receive: for as yet the Spirit had not been given, because Jesus was not yet glorified.",
  "7:40": "Of that crowd therefore, when they had heard these words of his, some said: This is the prophet indeed.",
  "7:42": "Does not the scripture say that the Christ comes from the seed of David and from Bethlehem, the town where David was?",
  "7:43": "So there arose a division among the people because of him.",
  "7:44": "And some of them wanted to seize him: but no one laid hands upon him.",
  "7:45": "The officers therefore came to the chief priests and the Pharisees. And they said to them: Why have you not brought him?",
  "7:46": "The officers answered: Never did any man speak like this man.",
  "7:47": "The Pharisees therefore answered them: Have you also been led astray?",
  "7:48": "Has any one of the rulers believed in him, or of the Pharisees?",
  "7:49": "But this crowd, which does not know the law, is accursed.",
  "7:50": "Nicodemus said to them (he who came to him by night, who was one of them):",
  "7:51": "Does our law judge any man unless it first hears him and knows what he does?",
  "7:52": "They answered and said to him: Are you also a Galilean? Search the scriptures, and see that no prophet rises out of Galilee.",
  "7:53": "And everyone returned to his own house.",
  "8:3": "And the scribes and Pharisees brought to him a woman caught in adultery: and they set her in the midst,",
  "8:4": "And said to him: Master, this woman has just now been caught in adultery.",
  "8:6": "And this they said testing him, so that they might accuse him. But Jesus, bending down, wrote with his finger on the ground.",
  "8:7": "When therefore they kept on asking him, he straightened up and said to them: Whoever among you is without sin, let him be the first to cast a stone at her.",
  "8:8": "And again bending down, he wrote on the ground.",
  "8:9": "But when they heard this, they went out one by one, beginning with the eldest. And Jesus was left alone, with the woman standing in the midst.",
  "8:10": "Then Jesus, straightening up, said to her: Woman, where are those who accused you? Has no one condemned you?",
  "8:11": "She said: No one, Lord. And Jesus said: Neither will I condemn you. Go, and now sin no more.",
  "8:12": "Again therefore Jesus spoke to them, saying: I am the light of the world. Whoever follows me does not walk in darkness, but shall have the light of life.",
  "8:14": "Jesus answered and said to them: Although I give testimony of myself, my testimony is true: for I know where I came from and where I am going.",
  "8:15": "You judge according to the flesh: I do not judge anyone.",
  "8:16": "And if I do judge, my judgment is true: because I am not alone, but I and the Father who sent me.",
  "8:18": "I am one who gives testimony of myself: and the Father who sent me gives testimony of me.",
  "8:19": "They said therefore to him: Where is your Father? Jesus answered: You know neither me nor my Father. If you knew me, perhaps you would know my Father also.",
  "8:20": "These words Jesus spoke in the treasury, teaching in the temple: and no one laid hands on him, because his hour had not yet come.",
  "8:21": "Again therefore Jesus said to them: I am going away: and you shall seek me. And you shall die in your sin. Where I am going, you cannot come.",
  "8:22": "The Jews therefore said: Will he kill himself, because he said: Where I am going you cannot come?",
  "8:23": "And he said to them: You are from below: I am from above. You are of this world: I am not of this world.",
  "8:24": "Therefore I said to you that you shall die in your sins. For if you do not believe that I am he, you shall die in your sin.",
  "8:25": "They said therefore to him: Who are you? Jesus said to them: The beginning, who also speak to you.",
  "8:26": "I have many things to say and to judge about you. But he who sent me is true: and the things I have heard from him, these same I speak in the world.",
  "8:27": "And they did not understand that he was calling God his Father.",
  "8:28": "Jesus therefore said to them: When you have lifted up the Son of man, then you shall know that I am he and that I do nothing of myself. But as the Father has taught me, these things I speak.",
  "8:29": "And he who sent me is with me: and he has not left me alone. For I always do the things that please him.",
  "8:30": "As he spoke these things, many believed in him.",
  "8:33": "They answered him: We are the seed of Abraham: and we have never been slaves to anyone. How can you say: You shall be free?",
  "8:35": "Now the servant does not remain in the house for ever: but the son remains for ever.",
  "8:36": "If therefore the Son makes you free, you shall be free indeed.",
  "8:38": "I speak what I have seen with my Father: and you do the things that you have seen with your father.",
  "8:39": "They answered and said to him: Abraham is our father. Jesus said to them: If you are the children of Abraham, do the works of Abraham.",
  "8:40": "But now you seek to kill me, a man who has spoken the truth to you, which I have heard from God. Abraham did not do this.",
  "8:41": "You do the works of your father. They said therefore to him: We were not born of fornication: we have one Father, God.",
  "8:42": "Jesus therefore said to them: If God were your Father, you would indeed love me. For from God I proceeded and came. For I did not come of myself: but he sent me.",
  "8:44": "You are of your father the devil: and the desires of your father you want to do. He was a murderer from the beginning: and he did not stand in the truth, because truth is not in him. When he tells a lie, he speaks from his own nature: for he is a liar, and the father of lies.",
  "8:45": "But because I tell the truth, you do not believe me.",
  "8:46": "Which of you shall convict me of sin? If I tell you the truth, why do you not believe me?",
  "8:47": "Whoever is of God hears the words of God. That is why you do not hear them, because you are not of God.",
  "8:48": "The Jews therefore answered and said to him: Are we not right in saying that you are a Samaritan and have a devil?",
  "8:49": "Jesus answered: I do not have a devil: but I honor my Father. And you have dishonored me.",
  "8:50": "But I do not seek my own glory: there is one who seeks it and judges.",
  "8:51": "Amen, amen, I say to you: If anyone keeps my word, he shall not see death for ever.",
  "8:52": "The Jews therefore said: Now we know that you have a devil. Abraham is dead, and the prophets: and you say: If anyone keeps my word, he shall not taste death for ever.",
  "8:53": "Are you greater than our father Abraham, who is dead? And the prophets are dead. Who do you make yourself out to be?",
  "8:54": "Jesus answered: If I glorify myself, my glory is nothing. It is my Father who glorifies me, of whom you say that he is your God.",
  "8:55": "And you have not known him: but I know him. And if I should say that I do not know him, I would be like you, a liar. But I do know him and I keep his word.",
  "9:1": "And Jesus, passing by, saw a man who was blind from his birth.",
  "9:3": "Jesus answered: Neither has this man sinned, nor his parents; but it is so that the works of God may be made known in him.",
  "9:4": "I must work the works of him who sent me while it is day: the night is coming, when no one can work.",
  "9:6": "When he had said these things, he spat on the ground and made clay from the spittle and spread the clay upon his eyes,",
  "9:7": "And said to him: Go, wash in the pool of Siloe, which means Sent. He went therefore and washed: and he came back seeing.",
  "9:8": "The neighbors therefore, and those who had seen him before as a beggar, said: Is not this the one who sat and begged? Some said: This is he.",
  "9:11": "He answered: The man who is called Jesus made clay and anointed my eyes and said to me: Go to the pool of Siloe and wash. And I went: I washed: and I see.",
  "9:12": "And they said to him: Where is he? He said: I do not know.",
  "9:13": "They brought the man who had been blind to the Pharisees.",
  "9:16": "Some therefore of the Pharisees said: This man is not from God, because he does not keep the sabbath. But others said: How can a man who is a sinner do such miracles? And there was a division among them.",
  "9:17": "They said therefore to the blind man again: What do you say about him who has opened your eyes? And he said: He is a prophet.",
  "9:18": "The Jews then did not believe about him that he had been blind and had received his sight, until they called the parents of the man who had received his sight,",
  "9:21": "But how he now sees, we do not know: or who has opened his eyes, we do not know. Ask him: he is of age: let him speak for himself.",
  "9:22": "These things his parents said because they feared the Jews: for the Jews had already agreed among themselves that if anyone should confess him to be the Christ, he should be put out of the synagogue.",
  "9:23": "That is why his parents said: He is of age. Ask him.",
  "9:24": "They therefore called again the man who had been blind and said to him: Give glory to God. We know that this man is a sinner.",
  "9:25": "He said therefore to them: Whether he is a sinner, I do not know. One thing I know, that though I was blind, now I see.",
  "9:26": "They said then to him: What did he do to you? How did he open your eyes?",
  "9:27": "He answered them: I have told you already, and you have heard. Why do you want to hear it again? Do you also want to become his disciples?",
  "9:28": "They insulted him therefore and said: You be his disciple; but we are the disciples of Moses.",
  "9:29": "We know that God spoke to Moses: but as for this man, we do not know where he is from.",
  "9:30": "The man answered and said to them: Why, this is a wonderful thing, that you do not know where he is from, and he has opened my eyes.",
  "9:31": "Now we know that God does not hear sinners: but if a man is a worshiper of God and does his will, him he hears.",
  "9:32": "Since the beginning of the world it has not been heard that anyone has opened the eyes of one born blind.",
  "9:33": "Unless this man were from God, he could not do anything.",
  "9:34": "They answered and said to him: You were wholly born in sins; and are you teaching us? And they cast him out.",
  "9:36": "He answered and said: Who is he, Lord, so that I may believe in him?",
  "9:37": "And Jesus said to him: You have both seen him; and it is he who is talking with you.",
  "9:39": "And Jesus said: For judgment I have come into this world: so that those who do not see may see; and those who see may become blind.",
  "9:40": "And some of the Pharisees who were with him heard this: and they said to him: Are we also blind?",
  "9:41": "Jesus said to them: If you were blind, you would not have sin: but now you say: We see. Your sin remains.",
  "10:1": "Amen, amen, I say to you: He who does not enter by the door into the sheepfold but climbs up another way is a thief and a robber.",
  "10:2": "But he who enters in by the door is the shepherd of the sheep.",
  "10:3": "To him the gatekeeper opens: and the sheep hear his voice. And he calls his own sheep by name and leads them out.",
  "10:5": "But a stranger they do not follow, but run away from him, because they do not know the voice of strangers.",
  "10:6": "This proverb Jesus spoke to them. But they did not understand what he was saying.",
  "10:8": "All others, as many as have come, are thieves and robbers: and the sheep did not hear them.",
  "10:9": "I am the door. By me, if anyone enters in, he shall be saved: and he shall go in and go out, and shall find pastures.",
  "10:10": "The thief comes only to steal and to kill and to destroy. I have come so that they may have life and may have it more abundantly.",
  "10:12": "But the hireling, who is not the shepherd and whose own the sheep are not, sees the wolf coming and leaves the sheep and runs away: and the wolf snatches and scatters the sheep.",
  "10:13": "And the hireling runs away because he is a hireling: and he does not care for the sheep.",
  "10:16": "And other sheep I have that are not of this fold: them also I must bring. And they shall hear my voice: and there shall be one fold and one shepherd.",
  "10:17": "That is why the Father loves me: because I lay down my life, so that I may take it up again.",
  "10:18": "No one takes it away from me: but I lay it down of myself. And I have power to lay it down: and I have power to take it up again. This commandment I have received from my Father.",
  "10:19": "A division arose again among the Jews because of these words.",
  "10:20": "And many of them said: He has a devil and is mad. Why do you listen to him?",
  "10:21": "Others said: These are not the words of one who has a devil. Can a devil open the eyes of the blind?",
  "10:24": "The Jews therefore gathered around him and said to him: How long will you keep us in suspense? If you are the Christ, tell us plainly.",
  "10:25": "Jesus answered them: I speak to you, and you do not believe: the works that I do in the name of my Father, they give testimony of me.",
  "10:28": "And I give them life everlasting: and they shall never perish. And no one shall snatch them out of my hand.",
  "10:29": "What my Father has given me is greater than all: and no one can snatch them out of the hand of my Father.",
  "10:32": "Jesus answered them: I have shown you many good works from my Father. For which of those works do you stone me?",
  "10:33": "The Jews answered him: We do not stone you for a good work, but for blasphemy: and because you, being a man, make yourself God.",
  "10:35": "If he called them gods to whom the word of God was spoken, and the scripture cannot be broken,",
  "10:37": "If I do not do the works of my Father, do not believe me.",
  "10:38": "But if I do, though you will not believe me, believe the works: so that you may know and believe that the Father is in me and I in the Father.",
  "10:39": "They tried therefore to seize him: and he escaped out of their hands.",
  "10:40": "And he went again beyond the Jordan, to the place where John was first baptizing. And there he stayed.",
  "10:41": "And many came to him: and they said: John indeed did no sign.",
  "10:42": "But all the things that John said about this man were true. And many believed in him.",
  "11:1": "Now there was a certain man who was sick, named Lazarus, of Bethania, the town of Mary and of Martha her sister.",
  "11:2": "(And Mary was the one who anointed the Lord with ointment and wiped his feet with her hair: it was her brother Lazarus who was sick.)",
  "11:4": "And Jesus, hearing it, said to them: This sickness will not end in death, but is for the glory of God, so that the Son of God may be glorified by it.",
  "11:6": "When he had heard therefore that he was sick, he still stayed in the same place two days.",
  "11:8": "The disciples said to him: Rabbi, the Jews were just now seeking to stone you. And are you going there again?",
  "11:9": "Jesus answered: Are there not twelve hours in the day? If anyone walks in the day, he does not stumble, because he sees the light of this world:",
  "11:10": "But if he walks in the night, he stumbles, because the light is not in him.",
  "11:11": "These things he said; and after that he said to them: Lazarus our friend is sleeping: but I am going so that I may wake him out of sleep.",
  "11:12": "His disciples therefore said: Lord, if he is sleeping, he will get well.",
  "11:13": "But Jesus had spoken of his death: and they thought that he was speaking of the rest of sleep.",
  "11:15": "And I am glad for your sakes that I was not there, so that you may believe. But let us go to him.",
  "11:16": "Thomas therefore, who is called Didymus, said to his fellow disciples: Let us also go, so that we may die with him.",
  "11:17": "Jesus therefore came: and found that he had already been in the grave four days.",
  "11:18": "(Now Bethania was near Jerusalem, about fifteen furlongs away.)",
  "11:19": "And many of the Jews had come to Martha and Mary to comfort them about their brother.",
  "11:20": "Martha therefore, as soon as she heard that Jesus had come, went to meet him: but Mary sat at home.",
  "11:21": "Martha therefore said to Jesus: Lord, if you had been here, my brother would not have died.",
  "11:22": "But even now I know that whatever you ask of God, God will give it to you.",
  "11:23": "Jesus said to her: Your brother shall rise again.",
  "11:24": "Martha said to him: I know that he shall rise again, in the resurrection on the last day.",
  "11:25": "Jesus said to her: I am the resurrection and the life: whoever believes in me, even if he dies, shall live:",
  "11:26": "And everyone who lives and believes in me shall never die. Do you believe this?",
  "11:27": "She said to him: Yes, Lord, I have believed that you are the Christ, the Son of the living God, who has come into this world.",
  "11:28": "And when she had said these things, she went and called her sister Mary secretly, saying: The master has come and is calling for you.",
  "11:29": "She, as soon as she heard this, rose quickly and came to him.",
  "11:30": "For Jesus had not yet come into the town: but he was still in the place where Martha had met him.",
  "11:31": "The Jews therefore who were with her in the house comforting her, when they saw that Mary rose up quickly and went out, followed her, saying: She is going to the grave to weep there.",
  "11:32": "When Mary therefore had come to where Jesus was, seeing him, she fell down at his feet and said to him: Lord, if you had been here, my brother would not have died.",
  "11:33": "Jesus therefore, when he saw her weeping, and the Jews who had come with her weeping, groaned in the spirit and was troubled,",
  "11:34": "And said: Where have you laid him? They said to him: Lord, come and see.",
  "11:37": "But some of them said: Could not he who opened the eyes of the man born blind have kept this man from dying?",
  "11:38": "Jesus therefore, again groaning in himself, came to the tomb. Now it was a cave; and a stone was laid over it.",
  "11:39": "Jesus said: Take away the stone. Martha, the sister of the dead man, said to him: Lord, by this time there will be a smell, for he has been dead four days.",
  "11:40": "Jesus said to her: Did I not say to you that if you believe, you shall see the glory of God?",
  "11:41": "They took the stone away therefore. And Jesus, lifting up his eyes, said: Father, I give you thanks that you have heard me.",
  "11:42": "And I knew that you always hear me: but I have said it because of the people who stand around, so that they may believe that you have sent me.",
  "11:43": "When he had said these things, he cried out with a loud voice: Lazarus, come forth.",
  "11:44": "And at once he who had been dead came forth, bound feet and hands with burial bands. And his face was bound around with a cloth. Jesus said to them: Untie him and let him go.",
  "11:45": "Many therefore of the Jews who had come to Mary and Martha and had seen the things that Jesus did believed in him.",
  "11:47": "The chief priests therefore and the Pharisees gathered a council and said: What are we doing? For this man does many miracles.",
  "11:48": "If we leave him alone like this, all will believe in him; and the Romans will come and take away our place and nation.",
  "11:49": "But one of them, named Caiphas, being the high priest that year, said to them: You know nothing.",
  "11:50": "Nor do you consider that it is better for you that one man should die for the people, and that the whole nation should not perish.",
  "11:51": "And this he did not say of himself: but being the high priest of that year, he prophesied that Jesus should die for the nation.",
  "11:52": "And not only for the nation, but to gather together in one the children of God who were scattered.",
  "11:53": "From that day therefore they plotted to put him to death.",
  "11:54": "Therefore Jesus no longer walked openly among the Jews: but he went into a country near the desert, to a city called Ephrem. And there he stayed with his disciples.",
  "11:56": "They were looking for Jesus therefore; and they said to one another, standing in the temple: What do you think? Will he not come to the festival day? And the chief priests and Pharisees had given an order that if anyone knew where he was, he should report it, so that they might seize him.",
  "12:2": "And they made him a supper there: and Martha served. But Lazarus was one of those who were at table with him.",
  "12:3": "Mary therefore took a pound of ointment of pure spikenard, of great price, and anointed the feet of Jesus and wiped his feet with her hair. And the house was filled with the fragrance of the ointment.",
  "12:4": "Then one of his disciples, Judas Iscariot, the one who was about to betray him, said:",
  "12:6": "Now he said this not because he cared for the poor; but because he was a thief and, having the purse, used to carry off what was put into it.",
  "12:7": "Jesus therefore said: Let her alone, so that she may keep it for the day of my burial.",
  "12:8": "For the poor you always have with you: but you do not always have me.",
  "12:9": "A great crowd of the Jews therefore learned that he was there; and they came, not for Jesus' sake only, but so that they might see Lazarus, whom he had raised from the dead.",
  "12:10": "But the chief priests planned to kill Lazarus also,",
  "12:11": "Because on account of him many of the Jews were going away and believing in Jesus.",
  "12:12": "And on the next day, a great crowd that had come to the festival day, when they heard that Jesus was coming to Jerusalem,",
  "12:13": "Took branches of palm trees and went out to meet him and cried: Hosanna! Blessed is he who comes in the name of the Lord, the king of Israel.",
  "12:14": "And Jesus found a young donkey and sat upon it, as it is written:",
  "12:15": "Fear not, daughter of Sion: behold, your king comes, sitting on a donkey's colt.",
  "12:16": "His disciples did not understand these things at first: but when Jesus was glorified, then they remembered that these things were written of him and that they had done these things to him.",
  "12:17": "The crowd therefore which was with him when he called Lazarus out of the grave and raised him from the dead gave testimony.",
  "12:18": "For this reason also the people came to meet him, because they heard that he had done this miracle.",
  "12:19": "The Pharisees therefore said among themselves: Do you see that we are getting nowhere? Behold, the whole world has gone after him.",
  "12:21": "These therefore came to Philip, who was of Bethsaida of Galilee, and asked him, saying: Sir, we would like to see Jesus.",
  "12:22": "Philip came and told Andrew. Then Andrew and Philip told Jesus.",
  "12:23": "But Jesus answered them, saying: The hour has come for the Son of man to be glorified.",
  "12:24": "Amen, amen, I say to you, unless the grain of wheat falling into the ground dies,",
  "12:25": "It remains alone. But if it dies, it brings forth much fruit. Whoever loves his life shall lose it, and whoever hates his life in this world keeps it for life eternal.",
  "12:26": "If anyone serves me, let him follow me: and where I am, there also shall my servant be. If anyone serves me, my Father will honor him.",
  "12:27": "Now my soul is troubled. And what shall I say? Father, save me from this hour. But for this reason I came to this hour.",
  "12:29": "The crowd therefore that stood and heard said that it had thundered. Others said: An angel spoke to him.",
  "12:30": "Jesus answered and said: This voice did not come because of me, but for your sakes.",
  "12:32": "And I, if I am lifted up from the earth, will draw all things to myself.",
  "12:33": "(Now this he said, signifying what death he would die.)",
  "12:34": "The crowd answered him: We have heard out of the law that the Christ remains for ever. And how can you say: The Son of man must be lifted up? Who is this Son of man?",
  "12:35": "Jesus therefore said to them: Yet a little while the light is among you. Walk while you have the light, so that the darkness does not overtake you. And whoever walks in darkness does not know where he is going.",
  "12:36": "While you have the light, believe in the light, so that you may be the children of light. These things Jesus spoke: and he went away and hid himself from them.",
  "12:37": "And though he had done so many miracles before them, they did not believe in him,",
  "12:38": "So that the saying of Isaiah the prophet might be fulfilled, which he said: Lord, who has believed our report? And to whom has the arm of the Lord been revealed?",
  "12:40": "He has blinded their eyes and hardened their heart, so that they should not see with their eyes, nor understand with their heart and be converted, and I should heal them.",
  "12:41": "Isaiah said these things when he saw his glory and spoke of him.",
  "12:42": "However, many of the leading men also believed in him: but because of the Pharisees they did not confess him, so that they would not be put out of the synagogue.",
  "12:44": "But Jesus cried out and said: Whoever believes in me does not believe in me, but in him who sent me.",
  "12:45": "And whoever sees me sees him who sent me.",
  "12:46": "I have come as a light into the world, so that whoever believes in me may not remain in darkness.",
  "12:47": "And if anyone hears my words and does not keep them, I do not judge him: for I did not come to judge the world, but to save the world.",
  "12:48": "Whoever despises me and does not receive my words has one who judges him. The word that I have spoken, that shall judge him on the last day.",
  "12:49": "For I have not spoken of myself: but the Father who sent me, he gave me a commandment what I should say and what I should speak.",
  "13:1": "Before the festival day of the pasch, Jesus, knowing that his hour had come to pass out of this world to the Father, having loved his own who were in the world, loved them to the end.",
  "13:2": "And when supper was over (the devil having now put it into the heart of Judas Iscariot, the son of Simon, to betray him),",
  "13:3": "Knowing that the Father had given all things into his hands and that he came from God and was going to God,",
  "13:4": "He rose from supper and laid aside his garments and, having taken a towel, girded himself.",
  "13:5": "After that, he poured water into a basin and began to wash the feet of the disciples and to wipe them with the towel with which he was girded.",
  "13:6": "He came therefore to Simon Peter. And Peter said to him: Lord, do you wash my feet?",
  "13:7": "Jesus answered and said to him: What I do, you do not know now; but you shall know later.",
  "13:8": "Peter said to him: You shall never wash my feet. Jesus answered him: If I do not wash you, you shall have no part with me.",
  "13:9": "Simon Peter said to him: Lord, not only my feet, but also my hands and my head.",
  "13:10": "Jesus said to him: Whoever has bathed needs only to wash his feet, but is clean all over. And you are clean, but not all.",
  "13:11": "For he knew who it was that would betray him; that is why he said: You are not all clean.",
  "13:12": "Then after he had washed their feet and taken his garments, sitting down again, he said to them: Do you know what I have done to you?",
  "13:14": "If then I, being your Lord and Master, have washed your feet, you also ought to wash one another's feet.",
  "13:15": "For I have given you an example, so that as I have done to you, so you also should do.",
  "13:16": "Amen, amen, I say to you: The servant is not greater than his lord: nor is the apostle greater than he who sent him.",
  "13:18": "I am not speaking of you all: I know whom I have chosen. But it is so that the scripture may be fulfilled: He who eats bread with me shall lift up his heel against me.",
  "13:19": "I tell you now, before it happens, so that when it happens you may believe that I am he.",
  "13:20": "Amen, amen, I say to you, whoever receives anyone I send receives me: and whoever receives me receives him who sent me.",
  "13:22": "The disciples therefore looked at one another, unsure of whom he spoke.",
  "13:24": "Simon Peter therefore signaled to him and said to him: Who is it of whom he speaks?",
  "13:25": "He therefore, leaning on the breast of Jesus, said to him: Lord, who is it?",
  "13:26": "Jesus answered: It is he to whom I shall hand the bread I have dipped. And when he had dipped the bread, he gave it to Judas Iscariot, the son of Simon.",
  "13:27": "And after the morsel, Satan entered into him. And Jesus said to him: What you are going to do, do quickly.",
  "13:28": "Now no one at the table knew why he said this to him.",
  "13:29": "For some thought, because Judas had the purse, that Jesus had said to him: Buy the things we need for the festival day: or that he should give something to the poor.",
  "13:31": "When he therefore had gone out, Jesus said: Now is the Son of man glorified; and God is glorified in him.",
  "13:32": "If God is glorified in him, God also will glorify him in himself: and he will glorify him at once.",
  "13:33": "Little children, yet a little while I am with you. You shall seek me. And as I said to the Jews: Where I am going you cannot come; so I say to you now.",
  "13:34": "A new commandment I give to you: that you love one another; as I have loved you, that you also love one another.",
  "13:35": "By this all men shall know that you are my disciples, if you have love for one another.",
  "13:36": "Simon Peter said to him: Lord, where are you going? Jesus answered: Where I am going, you cannot follow me now: but you shall follow later.",
  "13:37": "Peter said to him: Why can I not follow you now? I will lay down my life for you.",
  "13:38": "Jesus answered him: Will you lay down your life for me? Amen, amen, I say to you, the cock shall not crow until you deny me three times.",
  "14:3": "And if I go and prepare a place for you, I will come again and will take you to myself: so that where I am, you also may be.",
  "14:4": "And where I am going you know: and the way you know.",
  "14:5": "Thomas said to him: Lord, we do not know where you are going. And how can we know the way?",
  "14:6": "Jesus said to him: I am the way, and the truth, and the life. No one comes to the Father except by me.",
  "14:7": "If you had known me, you would surely have known my Father also: and from now on you shall know him. And you have seen him.",
  "14:8": "Philip said to him: Lord, show us the Father; and it is enough for us.",
  "14:9": "Jesus said to him: Have I been with you so long a time, and have you not known me? Philip, whoever sees me sees the Father also. How can you say: Show us the Father?",
  "14:10": "Do you not believe that I am in the Father and the Father in me? The words that I speak to you, I do not speak of myself. But the Father who abides in me, he does the works.",
  "14:11": "Do you not believe that I am in the Father and the Father in me?",
  "14:12": "Otherwise believe because of the works themselves. Amen, amen, I say to you, whoever believes in me, the works that I do, he also shall do: and greater than these he shall do. Because I am going to the Father.",
  "14:13": "And whatever you ask the Father in my name, that I will do: so that the Father may be glorified in the Son.",
  "14:14": "If you ask me anything in my name, I will do it.",
  "14:16": "And I will ask the Father: and he shall give you another Paraclete, to abide with you for ever:",
  "14:17": "The Spirit of truth, whom the world cannot receive, because it does not see him or know him. But you shall know him; because he shall abide with you and shall be in you.",
  "14:19": "Yet a little while and the world sees me no more. But you see me: because I live, you also shall live.",
  "14:20": "On that day you shall know that I am in my Father: and you in me, and I in you.",
  "14:21": "Whoever has my commandments and keeps them, he is the one who loves me. And whoever loves me shall be loved by my Father: and I will love him and will show myself to him.",
  "14:22": "Judas, not the Iscariot, said to him: Lord, how is it that you will show yourself to us, and not to the world?",
  "14:23": "Jesus answered and said to him: If anyone loves me, he will keep my word. And my Father will love him, and we will come to him and will make our home with him.",
  "14:24": "Whoever does not love me does not keep my words. And the word which you have heard is not mine, but the Father's who sent me.",
  "14:25": "These things I have spoken to you while abiding with you.",
  "14:26": "But the Paraclete, the Holy Spirit, whom the Father will send in my name, he will teach you all things and remind you of all things that I have said to you.",
  "14:27": "Peace I leave with you: my peace I give to you: not as the world gives do I give to you. Let not your heart be troubled: nor let it be afraid.",
  "14:28": "You have heard that I said to you: I am going away, and I am coming to you. If you loved me, you would indeed be glad, because I am going to the Father: for the Father is greater than I.",
  "14:29": "And now I have told you before it happens, so that when it happens you may believe.",
  "14:30": "I will not now speak many things with you. For the prince of this world is coming: and in me he has nothing.",
  "14:31": "But so that the world may know that I love the Father, and as the Father has given me commandment, so I do: Arise, let us go from here.",
  "15:1": "I am the true vine: and my Father is the vinedresser.",
  "15:2": "Every branch in me that does not bear fruit, he will take away: and every one that bears fruit, he will prune, so that it may bring forth more fruit.",
  "15:3": "Now you are clean because of the word which I have spoken to you.",
  "15:4": "Abide in me: and I in you. As the branch cannot bear fruit of itself unless it abides in the vine, so neither can you unless you abide in me.",
  "15:5": "I am the vine: you are the branches. Whoever abides in me, and I in him, bears much fruit: for without me you can do nothing.",
  "15:6": "If anyone does not abide in me, he shall be thrown out like a branch and shall wither: and they shall gather him up and cast him into the fire: and he burns.",
  "15:7": "If you abide in me and my words abide in you, you shall ask whatever you will: and it shall be done for you.",
  "15:8": "In this is my Father glorified: that you bring forth very much fruit and become my disciples.",
  "15:10": "If you keep my commandments, you shall abide in my love: just as I also have kept my Father's commandments and abide in his love.",
  "15:11": "These things I have spoken to you, so that my joy may be in you, and your joy may be full.",
  "15:13": "Greater love than this no one has, that a man lay down his life for his friends.",
  "15:16": "You have not chosen me: but I have chosen you; and have appointed you, that you should go and bring forth fruit, and your fruit should remain: so that whatever you ask of the Father in my name, he may give it to you.",
  "15:18": "If the world hates you, know that it has hated me before you.",
  "15:19": "If you were of the world, the world would love its own: but because you are not of the world, but I have chosen you out of the world, that is why the world hates you.",
  "15:21": "But all these things they will do to you for my name's sake: because they do not know him who sent me.",
  "15:23": "Whoever hates me hates my Father also.",
  "15:24": "If I had not done among them the works that no other man has done, they would not have sin: but now they have both seen and hated both me and my Father.",
  "15:25": "But this is so that the word may be fulfilled which is written in their law: They hated me without cause.",
  "15:27": "And you also shall give testimony, because you have been with me from the beginning.",
  "16:1": "These things I have spoken to you, so that you may not be scandalized.",
  "16:2": "They will put you out of the synagogues: yes, the hour is coming when whoever kills you will think that he is offering a service to God.",
  "16:3": "And these things they will do to you, because they have not known the Father nor me.",
  "16:4": "But these things I have told you, so that when the hour comes, you may remember that I told you of them.",
  "16:5": "But I did not tell you these things from the beginning, because I was with you. And now I am going to him who sent me, and none of you asks me: Where are you going?",
  "16:7": "But I tell you the truth: it is good for you that I go. For if I do not go, the Paraclete will not come to you: but if I go, I will send him to you.",
  "16:8": "And when he has come, he will convict the world of sin and of justice and of judgment.",
  "16:9": "Of sin: because they did not believe in me.",
  "16:10": "And of justice: because I am going to the Father: and you shall see me no longer.",
  "16:12": "I still have many things to say to you: but you cannot bear them now.",
  "16:13": "But when he, the Spirit of truth, has come, he will teach you all truth. For he shall not speak of himself: but whatever he hears, he shall speak. And the things that are to come, he shall show you.",
  "16:14": "He shall glorify me: because he shall receive of what is mine and shall show it to you.",
  "16:15": "All things that the Father has are mine. That is why I said that he shall receive of mine and show it to you.",
  "16:16": "A little while, and now you shall not see me: and again a little while, and you shall see me: because I am going to the Father.",
  "16:17": "Then some of his disciples said to one another: What is this that he says to us: A little while, and you shall not see me: and again a little while, and you shall see me; and, Because I am going to the Father?",
  "16:18": "They said therefore: What is this that he says, A little while? We do not know what he is talking about.",
  "16:19": "And Jesus knew that they wanted to ask him. And he said to them: Are you asking among yourselves about this, because I said: A little while, and you shall not see me; and again a little while, and you shall see me?",
  "16:21": "A woman, when she is in labor, has sorrow, because her hour has come; but when she has brought forth the child, she no longer remembers the anguish, for joy that a man is born into the world.",
  "16:22": "So also you now indeed have sorrow: but I will see you again and your heart shall rejoice. And your joy no one shall take from you.",
  "16:23": "And on that day you shall not ask me anything. Amen, amen, I say to you: if you ask the Father anything in my name, he will give it to you.",
  "16:24": "Until now you have not asked anything in my name. Ask, and you shall receive, so that your joy may be full.",
  "16:25": "These things I have spoken to you in proverbs. The hour is coming when I will no longer speak to you in proverbs, but will tell you plainly of the Father.",
  "16:26": "On that day you shall ask in my name: and I do not say to you that I will ask the Father for you.",
  "16:28": "I came forth from the Father and have come into the world: again I am leaving the world and going to the Father.",
  "16:29": "His disciples said to him: Behold, now you are speaking plainly and not in proverbs.",
  "16:30": "Now we know that you know all things and do not need anyone to ask you. By this we believe that you came forth from God.",
  "16:32": "Behold, the hour is coming, and has now come, when you shall be scattered, each to his own, and shall leave me alone. And yet I am not alone, because the Father is with me.",
  "16:33": "These things I have spoken to you, so that in me you may have peace. In the world you shall have distress. But have confidence: I have overcome the world.",
  "17:1": "These things Jesus spoke: and lifting up his eyes to heaven, he said: Father, the hour has come. Glorify your Son, so that your Son may glorify you.",
  "17:5": "And now glorify me, O Father, with yourself, with the glory which I had with you before the world was.",
  "17:6": "I have made your name known to the men whom you have given me out of the world. Yours they were: and to me you gave them. And they have kept your word.",
  "17:8": "Because the words which you gave me, I have given to them. And they have received them and have truly known that I came out from you: and they have believed that you sent me.",
  "17:9": "I pray for them. I do not pray for the world, but for those whom you have given me: because they are yours.",
  "17:10": "And all my things are yours, and yours are mine: and I am glorified in them.",
  "17:11": "And now I am no longer in the world, and these are in the world, and I am coming to you. Holy Father, keep them in your name whom you have given me, so that they may be one, as we also are.",
  "17:12": "While I was with them, I kept them in your name. Those whom you gave me I have kept: and none of them is lost except the son of perdition, so that the scripture may be fulfilled.",
  "17:13": "And now I am coming to you: and these things I speak in the world, so that they may have my joy made full in themselves.",
  "17:15": "I do not pray that you should take them out of the world, but that you should keep them from evil.",
  "17:19": "And for them I sanctify myself, so that they also may be sanctified in truth.",
  "17:20": "And not for them only do I pray, but for those also who through their word shall believe in me:",
  "17:21": "That they all may be one, as you, Father, in me, and I in you; that they also may be one in us: so that the world may believe that you have sent me.",
  "17:22": "And the glory which you have given me, I have given to them, so that they may be one, as we also are one:",
  "17:23": "I in them, and you in me, so that they may be made perfect in one: and the world may know that you have sent me and have loved them, as you have also loved me.",
  "17:24": "Father, I will that where I am, those also whom you have given me may be with me, so that they may see my glory which you have given me, because you loved me before the creation of the world.",
  "18:1": "When Jesus had said these things, he went out with his disciples across the brook Cedron, where there was a garden, into which he entered with his disciples.",
  "18:2": "And Judas also, who betrayed him, knew the place: because Jesus had often gone there with his disciples.",
  "18:3": "Judas therefore, having received a band of soldiers and servants from the chief priests and the Pharisees, came there with lanterns and torches and weapons.",
  "18:4": "Jesus therefore, knowing all the things that were to come upon him, went out and said to them: Whom are you looking for?",
  "18:5": "They answered him: Jesus of Nazareth. Jesus said to them: I am he. And Judas also, who betrayed him, was standing with them.",
  "18:7": "Again therefore he asked them: Whom are you looking for? And they said: Jesus of Nazareth.",
  "18:8": "Jesus answered: I have told you that I am he. If therefore you are looking for me, let these go their way,",
  "18:9": "So that the word might be fulfilled which he said: Of those whom you have given me, I have not lost any.",
  "18:10": "Then Simon Peter, having a sword, drew it and struck the servant of the high priest and cut off his right ear. And the name of the servant was Malchus.",
  "18:11": "Jesus therefore said to Peter: Put your sword back into the scabbard. The chalice which my Father has given me, shall I not drink it?",
  "18:12": "Then the band of soldiers and the tribune and the servants of the Jews took Jesus and bound him.",
  "18:14": "Now Caiphas was the one who had advised the Jews that it was better for one man to die for the people.",
  "18:15": "And Simon Peter followed Jesus: and so did another disciple. And that disciple was known to the high priest and went in with Jesus into the courtyard of the high priest.",
  "18:16": "But Peter stood outside at the door. The other disciple therefore, who was known to the high priest, went out and spoke to the doorkeeper and brought Peter in.",
  "18:17": "The servant girl therefore who was the doorkeeper said to Peter: Are you not also one of this man's disciples? He said: I am not.",
  "18:18": "Now the servants and officers were standing at a charcoal fire, because it was cold, and were warming themselves. And Peter also was with them, standing and warming himself.",
  "18:19": "The high priest therefore asked Jesus about his disciples and about his teaching.",
  "18:20": "Jesus answered him: I have spoken openly to the world. I have always taught in the synagogue and in the temple, where all the Jews gather: and in secret I have spoken nothing.",
  "18:21": "Why do you ask me? Ask those who have heard what I have spoken to them. Behold, they know what I have said.",
  "18:22": "And when he had said these things, one of the officers standing by struck Jesus a blow, saying: Is that how you answer the high priest?",
  "18:25": "And Simon Peter was standing and warming himself. They said therefore to him: Are you not also one of his disciples? He denied it and said: I am not.",
  "18:26": "One of the servants of the high priest (a relative of the man whose ear Peter cut off) said to him: Did I not see you in the garden with him?",
  "18:27": "Again therefore Peter denied it: and immediately the cock crowed.",
  "18:28": "Then they led Jesus from Caiphas to the governor's hall. And it was morning: and they did not go into the hall, so that they would not be defiled, but might eat the pasch.",
  "18:29": "Pilate therefore went out to them and said: What accusation do you bring against this man?",
  "18:30": "They answered and said to him: If he were not a criminal, we would not have handed him over to you.",
  "18:31": "Pilate therefore said to them: You take him and judge him according to your law. The Jews therefore said to him: It is not lawful for us to put anyone to death.",
  "18:32": "This was so that the word of Jesus might be fulfilled, which he said, signifying what death he would die.",
  "18:34": "Jesus answered: Do you say this of yourself, or have others told you about me?",
  "18:35": "Pilate answered: Am I a Jew? Your own nation and the chief priests have handed you over to me. What have you done?",
  "18:36": "Jesus answered: My kingdom is not of this world. If my kingdom were of this world, my servants would certainly fight so that I would not be handed over to the Jews: but now my kingdom is not from here.",
  "18:37": "Pilate therefore said to him: Are you a king then? Jesus answered: You say that I am a king. For this I was born, and for this I came into the world: to give testimony to the truth. Everyone who is of the truth hears my voice.",
  "18:38": "Pilate said to him: What is truth? And when he had said this, he went out again to the Jews and said to them: I find no cause in him.",
  "18:39": "But you have a custom that I should release one to you at the pasch. Do you want me, therefore, to release to you the king of the Jews?",
  "18:40": "Then they all cried out again, saying: Not this man, but Barabbas. Now Barabbas was a robber.",
  "19:2": "And the soldiers, weaving a crown of thorns, put it upon his head: and they put a purple garment on him.",
  "19:3": "And they came to him and said: Hail, king of the Jews. And they struck him with their hands.",
  "19:4": "Pilate therefore went out again and said to them: Behold, I bring him out to you, so that you may know that I find no cause in him.",
  "19:5": "(Jesus therefore came out, wearing the crown of thorns and the purple garment.) And he said to them: Behold the Man.",
  "19:6": "When the chief priests therefore and the officers had seen him, they cried out, saying: Crucify him, crucify him. Pilate said to them: You take him and crucify him: for I find no cause in him.",
  "19:8": "When Pilate therefore heard this saying, he was all the more afraid.",
  "19:9": "And he went into the hall again; and he said to Jesus: Where are you from? But Jesus gave him no answer.",
  "19:10": "Pilate therefore said to him: Do you not speak to me? Do you not know that I have power to crucify you, and I have power to release you?",
  "19:11": "Jesus answered: You would not have any power against me unless it were given to you from above. Therefore he who has handed me over to you has the greater sin.",
  "19:12": "And from then on Pilate tried to release him. But the Jews cried out, saying: If you release this man, you are not Caesar's friend. For whoever makes himself a king speaks against Caesar.",
  "19:13": "Now when Pilate had heard these words, he brought Jesus out and sat down in the judgment seat, in the place that is called Lithostrotos, and in Hebrew Gabbatha.",
  "19:14": "And it was the parasceve of the pasch, about the sixth hour: and he said to the Jews: Behold your king.",
  "19:15": "But they cried out: Away with him: away with him: crucify him. Pilate said to them: Shall I crucify your king? The chief priests answered: We have no king but Caesar.",
  "19:16": "Then therefore he handed him over to them to be crucified. And they took Jesus and led him out.",
  "19:17": "And carrying his own cross, he went out to the place which is called Calvary, but in Hebrew Golgotha,",
  "19:19": "And Pilate also wrote a title: and he put it upon the cross. And the writing was: JESUS OF NAZARETH, THE KING OF THE JEWS.",
  "19:20": "This title therefore many of the Jews read: because the place where Jesus was crucified was near the city. And it was written in Hebrew, in Greek, and in Latin.",
  "19:21": "Then the chief priests of the Jews said to Pilate: Do not write: The King of the Jews. But that he said: I am the King of the Jews.",
  "19:23": "The soldiers therefore, when they had crucified him, took his garments (and they made four parts, to every soldier a part) and also his coat. Now the coat was without seam, woven from the top throughout.",
  "19:24": "They said then to one another: Let us not tear it, but let us cast lots for it, to see whose it shall be; so that the scripture might be fulfilled, which says: They have divided my garments among them, and upon my clothing they have cast lots. And the soldiers indeed did these things.",
  "19:25": "Now there stood by the cross of Jesus his mother and his mother's sister, Mary of Cleophas, and Mary Magdalene.",
  "19:26": "When Jesus therefore had seen his mother and the disciple standing whom he loved, he said to his mother: Woman, behold your son.",
  "19:27": "After that, he said to the disciple: Behold your mother. And from that hour, the disciple took her to his own.",
  "19:28": "Afterwards, Jesus, knowing that all things were now accomplished, so that the scripture might be fulfilled, said: I thirst.",
  "19:29": "Now there was a vessel set there, full of vinegar. And they, putting a sponge full of vinegar on hyssop, put it to his mouth.",
  "19:31": "Then the Jews (because it was the parasceve), so that the bodies might not remain upon the cross on the sabbath day (for that was a great sabbath day), asked Pilate that their legs might be broken and that they might be taken away.",
  "19:32": "The soldiers therefore came: and they broke the legs of the first, and of the other who was crucified with him.",
  "19:33": "But when they came to Jesus and saw that he was already dead, they did not break his legs.",
  "19:35": "And he who saw it has given testimony: and his testimony is true. And he knows that he tells the truth, so that you also may believe.",
  "19:36": "For these things were done so that the scripture might be fulfilled: You shall not break a bone of him.",
  "19:38": "And after these things, Joseph of Arimathea (because he was a disciple of Jesus, but secretly for fear of the Jews) asked Pilate that he might take away the body of Jesus. And Pilate gave permission. He came therefore and took away the body of Jesus.",
  "19:39": "And Nicodemus also came (he who at first came to Jesus by night), bringing a mixture of myrrh and aloes, about a hundred pounds in weight.",
  "19:40": "They took therefore the body of Jesus and bound it in linen cloths with the spices, as is the custom of the Jews in burying.",
  "19:41": "Now in the place where he was crucified there was a garden: and in the garden a new tomb, in which no one had yet been laid.",
  "19:42": "There, therefore, because of the parasceve of the Jews, they laid Jesus: because the tomb was near at hand.",
  "20:1": "And on the first day of the week, Mary Magdalene came early, while it was still dark, to the tomb: and she saw the stone taken away from the tomb.",
  "20:2": "She ran therefore and came to Simon Peter and to the other disciple whom Jesus loved and said to them: They have taken the Lord out of the tomb: and we do not know where they have laid him.",
  "20:4": "And they both ran together: and that other disciple outran Peter and came first to the tomb.",
  "20:5": "And when he stooped down, he saw the linen cloths lying there: but he did not go in.",
  "20:6": "Then Simon Peter came, following him, and went into the tomb: and saw the linen cloths lying there,",
  "20:7": "And the cloth that had been about his head, not lying with the linen cloths, but rolled up in a place by itself.",
  "20:9": "For as yet they did not know the scripture, that he must rise again from the dead.",
  "20:10": "The disciples therefore went back again to their home.",
  "20:11": "But Mary stood outside the tomb, weeping. Now as she was weeping, she stooped down and looked into the tomb,",
  "20:13": "They said to her: Woman, why are you weeping? She said to them: Because they have taken away my Lord: and I do not know where they have laid him.",
  "20:14": "When she had said this, she turned around and saw Jesus standing: and she did not know that it was Jesus.",
  "20:15": "Jesus said to her: Woman, why are you weeping? Whom are you looking for? She, thinking that it was the gardener, said to him: Sir, if you have carried him away, tell me where you have laid him: and I will take him away.",
  "20:16": "Jesus said to her: Mary. She turned and said to him: Rabboni (which means Master).",
  "20:17": "Jesus said to her: Do not touch me: for I have not yet ascended to my Father. But go to my brothers and say to them: I ascend to my Father and to your Father, to my God and to your God.",
  "20:18": "Mary Magdalene came and told the disciples: I have seen the Lord; and these things he said to me.",
  "20:19": "Now when it was late that same day, the first day of the week, and the doors were shut where the disciples were gathered together for fear of the Jews, Jesus came and stood in their midst and said to them: Peace be to you.",
  "20:20": "And when he had said this, he showed them his hands and his side. The disciples therefore were glad when they saw the Lord.",
  "20:22": "When he had said this, he breathed on them; and he said to them: Receive the Holy Spirit.",
  "20:25": "The other disciples therefore said to him: We have seen the Lord. But he said to them: Unless I see in his hands the print of the nails and put my finger into the place of the nails and put my hand into his side, I will not believe.",
  "20:26": "And after eight days, his disciples were again inside, and Thomas with them. Jesus came, the doors being shut, and stood in their midst and said: Peace be to you.",
  "20:27": "Then he said to Thomas: Put your finger here and see my hands. And bring your hand here and put it into my side. And do not be faithless, but believing.",
  "20:29": "Jesus said to him: Because you have seen me, Thomas, you have believed: blessed are they who have not seen and have believed.",
  "20:30": "Jesus also did many other signs in the sight of his disciples, which are not written in this book.",
  "20:31": "But these are written so that you may believe that Jesus is the Christ, the Son of God: and that believing, you may have life in his name.",
  "21:1": "After this, Jesus showed himself again to the disciples at the sea of Tiberias. And he showed himself in this way.",
  "21:2": "There were together Simon Peter and Thomas, who is called Didymus, and Nathanael, who was of Cana of Galilee, and the sons of Zebedee and two others of his disciples.",
  "21:3": "Simon Peter said to them: I am going fishing. They said to him: We also are coming with you. And they went out and got into the boat: and that night they caught nothing.",
  "21:4": "But when morning had come, Jesus stood on the shore: yet the disciples did not know that it was Jesus.",
  "21:5": "Jesus therefore said to them: Children, do you have any food? They answered him: No.",
  "21:6": "He said to them: Cast the net on the right side of the boat, and you shall find. They cast it therefore: and now they were not able to haul it in, because of the great number of fish.",
  "21:7": "That disciple therefore whom Jesus loved said to Peter: It is the Lord. Simon Peter, when he heard that it was the Lord, put on his coat (for he was stripped) and threw himself into the sea.",
  "21:8": "But the other disciples came in the boat (for they were not far from the land, only about two hundred cubits), dragging the net full of fish.",
  "21:9": "As soon then as they came to land, they saw hot coals lying there, and a fish laid on them, and bread.",
  "21:10": "Jesus said to them: Bring some of the fish which you have just caught.",
  "21:11": "Simon Peter went up and drew the net to land, full of large fish, one hundred and fifty-three. And although there were so many, the net was not torn.",
  "21:12": "Jesus said to them: Come and eat. And none of those who were at table dared ask him: Who are you? knowing that it was the Lord.",
  "21:13": "And Jesus came and took bread and gave it to them: and the fish in the same way.",
  "21:14": "This was now the third time that Jesus showed himself to his disciples after he had risen from the dead.",
  "21:15": "When therefore they had eaten, Jesus said to Simon Peter: Simon, son of John, do you love me more than these? He said to him: Yes, Lord, you know that I love you. He said to him: Feed my lambs.",
  "21:16": "He said to him again: Simon, son of John, do you love me? He said to him: Yes, Lord, you know that I love you. He said to him: Feed my lambs.",
  "21:18": "Amen, amen, I say to you, when you were younger, you girded yourself and walked where you would. But when you are old, you shall stretch out your hands, and another shall gird you and lead you where you would not.",
  "21:19": "And this he said, signifying by what death he would glorify God. And when he had said this, he said to him: Follow me.",
  "21:20": "Peter, turning around, saw that disciple whom Jesus loved following, who also leaned on his breast at supper and said: Lord, who is it that shall betray you?",
  "21:21": "When Peter saw him, he said to Jesus: Lord, and what shall this man do?",
  "21:22": "Jesus said to him: If I will have him remain until I come, what is it to you? You follow me.",
  "21:23": "This saying therefore went out among the brothers, that that disciple would not die. And Jesus did not say to him: He shall not die; but: If I will have him remain until I come, what is it to you?",
  "21:25": "But there are also many other things which Jesus did, which, if they were written every one, the world itself, I think, would not be able to contain the books that would be written.",
};
